                        "entry_id": "cc1e08c5-076a-3234-9ae1-f1bd7030ddee",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Body of persons, such as priests, who are trained and ordained for religious service."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "77aaf779-7ba3-47f8-9dc3-9a00667cc8d1",
                                "sense_id": "81e487eb-aaf2-3550-9989-f86cdc3f03ce",
                                "text": "Today we brought together clergy from the Anglican, Catholic, Orthodox, and Reformed traditions for ecumenical dialogue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2f187d88-5e73-4bfb-b681-34cbead7535f",
                                "sense_id": "81e487eb-aaf2-3550-9989-f86cdc3f03ce",
                                "text": "Then everybody once more knelt, and soon the blessing was pronounced. The choir and the clergy trooped out slowly, […], down the nave to the western door. […] At a seemingly immense distance the surpliced group stopped to say the last prayer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "96430d3d-328a-41f4-9071-5709c087df34",
                                "sense_id": "81e487eb-aaf2-3550-9989-f86cdc3f03ce",
                                "text": "After years of debate, hundreds of United Methodists from all over the world gathered in St. Louis last week to settle the denomination’s stance on LGBT clergy and same-sex weddings."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
